## 12. Expected Business Outcomes

The proposed analytical framework is expected to provide the following outcomes:

### 12.1 Improved Delivery Monitoring

The analysis can help logistics managers monitor delivery-time deviation and ETA variation and identify operational conditions associated with delays.

### 12.2 Early Risk Identification

Risk-related analysis can help identify logistics operations that require additional monitoring or intervention.

### 12.3 Better Resource Allocation

Insights from demand, inventory, route risk, and operational conditions can support better allocation of vehicles, warehouse resources, and delivery capacity.

### 12.4 Cost Management

Analysis of shipping costs, fuel consumption, and route-related factors can help identify opportunities for transportation cost reduction.

### 12.5 Improved Operational Planning

Predictive analytics can support proactive planning rather than relying entirely on reactive responses after delays occur.

### 12.6 Logistics Segmentation

Clustering can identify groups of operations with similar characteristics, allowing managers to apply different strategies to different operational segments.

